From b84724bb70283d5f8d4e17c79f88baf6597ccccc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JimmyBlunt <jo@paso-music.de>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:21:25 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] Add FastLED Pattern engine: marker, wasm host, handle,
 controls (local #9002)

A Pattern whose leading comment block carries `// @pxlblz-language fastled`
is a FastLED Pattern (C++ against FastLED). patternLanguage.ts detects the
marker and the optional `@pxlblz-dim` / `@pxlblz-output` directives.

- fastledWasmHost.ts: vendored verbatim from fastled-integration
  runtime/fastledWasmHost.ts (host ABI 1), provenance header only.
- fastledPatternHandle.ts: a PatternHandle over the host. beforeRender(dt)
  runs frame(dt) (first frame(0) once, later zero deltas re-emit), render*
  emits byte/255 of L2 wire bytes (default) or L1 leds[] through rgb().
- fastledControls.ts: UISlider/UINumberField/UICheckbox -> ranged Controls,
  persisted values keyed by FastLED UI name (clamped, unknown keys ignored).
- PatternMetadata controls gain an optional `range` (FastLED only).
- newFastLedPattern.ts: starter template using PXLBLZ_NUM_LEDS and UISliders.
- Fixtures: template + PipelineTest wasm with golden L1/L2 dumps from the
  native FastLED reference (scripts/generate-fastled-fixtures.mjs); the wasm
  test replays them through createRenderLoop + paintPacked: 0 differing bytes.

Pre-commit hook checks run manually (hook cannot spawn npx.cmd on Windows/Node 24):
npm run lint, check:e2e-coverage, check:e2e-locators, tsc -b (tsconfig + node),
vitest src/engine/patternLanguage.test.ts src/engine/fastled (40 passed).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
